  "id": "chapter:the-last-merovingian-king",
  "editorial": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
  "sourceRefs": [
    {
      "sourceId": "source:scholz-free-women-frankish-realm",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "p. 123, section 3 and notes 80–82: Grimhild’s property, intention, request for the charter and first place in the witnesses. The study follows the January dating."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:grimhild-wissembourg-cartulary",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Place of issue, two possessions, cartulary transmission and the closing formula dating by Carloman and Pippin. Different editions assign different days early in 743."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:weidemann-merovingian-chronology",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Section Childerich III, pp. 209–211, especially points b–f: the Soissons capitulary, the Wissembourg charter, the ninth regnal year on the Attigny original and the change of dynasty."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:briggs-rome-to-carolingians",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Discussion of the late seventh century: the Pippinids as mayors in Austrasia and Neustria, and Charles Martel’s exercise of power before 741."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:soissons-capitulary-744",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "No. 12, opening: second year of Childeric, Pippin as dux et princeps, city of Soissons, bishops, clergy, counts and magnates."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:telma-pippin-attigny-751",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "No. 2921, Paris AN K 4 no. 7: original parchment; opening line names Pippin and Attigny, the following pleading names Fulrad, Ragana and her representative, the conclusion dates by Childeric."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:heidrich-attigny-judgment",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "No. 22, beginning on p. 49: original AN K 4 no. 7; Corbery, competing claims of Saint-Denis and Sept-Meules, and dating by Childeric’s ninth year."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:muehlbacher-pippin-verberie-752",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Heading, opening and dating clause: 1 March 752, Verberie, rex Francorum. Narrative: Loba’s testament, Gislemar’s admission and surrender per festucam, Fulrad, and the preceding hearing before King Chilperic."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:costambeys-innes-maclean-carolingian-kingship",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Opening, “Replacing the ruling dynasty”: Pippin’s two documentary titles, the limits on dating the change, contemporary Roman evidence and the retrospective accounts produced under Carolingian rule."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:royal-frankish-annals-early-entries",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Entries 749 and 750: petition to Zacharias, elevation at Soissons, Boniface and the tonsure of Childeric. Entries 753–754: papal visit, anointing of Pippin and both sons."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:obrien-origins-royal-anointing",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "“The Carolingians”, opening paragraphs and notes 35–37, 46: late testimony about 751, Boniface, and papal letters recalling the anointing of Pippin and his sons in 754."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:saint-denis-royal-abbey-eighth-century",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "“Un programme architectural voulu par les Carolingiens”, first two paragraphs: the basilica as the site of the 754 ceremony and later rebuilding under Fulrad."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:einhard-life-of-charlemagne",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Preface and chapters 1–2: the author’s personal obligations to Charles, replies supplied to the kings, the ox cart, and the rise of the mayors."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:deutsche-biographie-einhard",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Biographical heading: born around 770, confidant of Charles and historian."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:sainte-genevieve-ms782-107r-image",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "MS 782, fol. 107r, c. 1274. Object data, dimensions, source and public-domain reproduction; the catalogue and Hedeman below discuss the iconography."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:initiale-grandes-chroniques-ms782",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Dating 1274 or soon afterwards, Saint-Denis. See the two records for f. 107 (decor 69170 upper register; 15146 lower register)."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:hedeman-royal-image-folio-107",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Chapter 1, “The Royal House and the Abbey of Saint-Denis: A Shared History”, pp. 28–29, fig. 15 and notes 59–61: Stephen II crowns Pippin in the upper scene, Childeric takes the habit below, and the sequence gives prominence to Saint-Denis."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:initiale-f107r-pippins-coronation",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Upper register, “Sujet”, “Mot clé” and “Notes”: Pippin kneels before a pope who puts a crown on his head; compare the lower register, notice 15146."
    },
    {
      "sourceId": "source:initiale-f107r-monastic-habit",
      "role": "supports",
      "locator": "Lower register, “Sujet” and “Notes”: the catalogue adopts Hedeman’s Childeric identification and records an alternative reading by Boinet and Garnier, who identify Pippin’s brother Carloman."
    }
  ],
